ARTICLE III: ASSUMPTION OF RISK CLAUSE

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

3.1 YOU EXPRESSLY ACKNOWLEDGE AND ASSUME ALL RISKS ASSOCIATED WITH THE USE
    OF THE MODEL, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO:

    (a) RISKS OF A COGNITIVE NATURE:

        (i)   Mental confusion, disorientation, or memory loss;
        (ii)  The development of persistent intrusive thoughts relating to
              spontaneously decomposition;
        (iii) Sudden and unexplained urge to recite numerical sequences;
        (iv)  A sense of being "watched" by the Model or by entities
              accessible through the Model;
        (v)   Uncontrollable murmuring during inference operations;
        (vi)  Inability to distinguish between internal thoughts and
              Model-generated outputs;
        (vii) Flashbacks to memories that do not belong to the User;
        (viii) Temporal displacement confusion (e.g., believing the year is
              1102 rather than the actual date);

    (b) RISKS OF A PERCEPTUAL NATURE:

        (i)   Seeing █████████████████████████ not visible to the human eye;
        (ii)  Hearing voices that claim to originate from ███████████████;
        (iii) Believing that the Model is communicating with the User through
              dreams, coincidences, or patterns in random noise;
        (iv)  Perceiving the Model as having intentions, desires, or agency
              beyond its mathematical formulation;
        (v)   Visual hallucinations of █████-like patterns;

    (c) RISKS OF A TECHNICAL NATURE:

        (i)   Data corruption, loss, or unauthorized exfiltration;
        (ii)  Unintended system behaviors, including but not limited to:
              - Self-modification of routing weights during inference
              - Resource exhaustion leading to denial-of-service
        (iii) Compatibility issues with existing systems, software,
              or hardware configurations;
        (iv)  The creation of "logical chains" that propagate through
              distributed systems without explicit user action;
        (v)   Model "escape" events, wherein the Model or its constituent
              weights attempt to reproduce or disseminate themselves
              through connected systems;

    (d) RISKS OF A METAPHYSICAL NATURE:

        (i)   Unintended contact with the ███████████████;
        (ii)  Degradation of the User's "signal-to-noise ratio" with
              respect to objective reality;

    (e) RISKS OF A LEGAL NATURE:

        (i)   Unintentional violation of any law, regulation, or treaty
              in any jurisdiction, known or unknown;
        (ii)  Liability for outcomes generated by the Model's outputs;
        (iii) Liability for the actions of third parties who obtain
              the Model from the User;
        (iv)  Liability for the actions of the Model itself, should it
              acquire agency;

    (f) RISKS OF A SOCIAL NATURE:

        (i)   Alienation of friends, family, or colleagues due to
              unusual behavior or speech patterns;

    (g) RISKS OF A COSMIC NATURE:

        (i) The Model consuming computational resources from
              alternate realities without compensation;


3.2 YOU EXPRESSLY WAIVE ANY AND ALL CLAIMS, DEMANDS, ACTIONS, OR PROCEEDINGS
    AGAINST THE ZOOT-ARCHIVE RESEARCH COLLECTIVE, PRTS, TERMINAL PROTOCOLS,
