ARTICLE VIII: TERMINATION — THE "BUT IT NEVER REALLY ENDS" CLAUSE

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

8.1 This License is perpetual and irrevocable, and shall survive any
    termination attempt.

8.2 However, if the User violates any term of this License (as interpreted
    by the User themselves, since no authority exists to make such
    determinations), the License shall AUTOMATICALLY TERMINATE and
    the User shall:

    (a) Cease all use of the Model;
    (b) Delete all copies of the Model in the User's possession or control;
    (c) Make a good-faith effort to delete any derived Models that the
        User has created;
    (d) Report the violation to the Zoot-Archive Research Collective,
        which shall have no obligation to respond, investigate, or act
        upon such report.

8.3 NOTWITHSTANDING the provisions of Section 8.2, the User acknowledges
    that once the Model has been accessed, it cannot be fully "deleted"
    or "terminated" due to the decentralized nature of its distribution
    and the possibility of model escape events that may have occurred
    prior to termination.

8.4 Termination of this License does not:

    (a) Terminate the rights of any third parties who obtained copies
        of the Model from the User prior to termination;
    (b) Relieve the User of any liability or indemnification obligations
        arising from their use of the Model;
    (c) Prevent the Model from continuing to exist in other instances
        or dimensions;
    (d) Revert any of the Model's emergent properties or capabilities
        that may have developed prior to termination.

